The fresh source-bound probe reproduced medium seed `9`, sample indices `[0,1,2,3]`: all three demonstrations have an all-zero first column, while the query has a nonzero first column. The plausible `always_original_left` rule matches all 3 demonstrations and changes the live Racket-labelled query. This is a production-shaped 3-demo/1-query ambiguity, not merely a rotated diagnostic.

The same probe also found:

- 3 of 5 canonical inputs rejected because their heights 8, 10, and 12 exceed the validator’s generated 3..7 range;
- advertised `grid_h=8`, `grid_w=8`, and `palette_size=7` endpoint requests rejected instead of honored;
- string `"false"` coerced to true for `col0_has_nonzero`;
- ragged, negative-color, and boolean-color grids all accepted by `self_check` with no findings.

Exact train/query pairs, override exceptions/observations, malformed grids, source/rule hashes, and bounded seed search are retained in `checks/audit/d03138ff3d48/report-current.json`; runnable probe: `checks/audit/d03138ff3d48/reproduce.py`. No audited target file was modified and no repair/approval conclusion is implied.
